{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Thyristor and GTO",
  "exampleId": "block-thyristors",
  "description": "Both switch a 10 V, 50 Hz sine into a 10 Ω load and are fired 2.5 ms into each cycle for 2 ms. The thyristor latches: once fired it conducts until its current reaches zero at the end of the positive half-cycle. The GTO stops conducting as soon as its gate goes off at 4.5 ms.",
